  "reason": "Completed experiments show that RNA PCA with multiprofile avgpool is the current best setting (0.591 accuracy, 0.573 F1), and avgpool multiprofile also improves image ResNet, so profile aggregation is a proven lever. The key uncertainty is whether a learned RNA representation improves over PCA under this same promising setting. config_005 tests scVI_n200 while keeping multiprofile avgpool fixed, isolating the RNA encoder effect. This is the best next use of budget because it is a one-factor extension of the current best, may raise the unimodal baseline before adding multimodal complexity, and will clarify whether representation learning is an important design choice for future multimodal models."
